.TH MFA-KEYRING 1 "2026-10-02" "mfa-keyring" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mfa-keyring \- unlock the GNOME keyring and ZFS home with a PIV card or FIDO2 key
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mfa-keyring
.RI [ options ]
.I command
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mfa-keyring enroll
changes the login keyring password to a random 256-bit secret and stores that
secret in a wrap file
.RI ( /var/lib/mfa-keyring/ user /login.wrap
if that directory exists, otherwise
.IR ~/.local/share/mfa-keyring/login.wrap ),
sealed to a PIV card key (default: the key management key, PKCS#11 id 03) or,
with
.BR \-\-fido2 ,
to a FIDO2 security key, and also to your login password so that password logins
keep working.
.BR pam_mfa_keyring (8)
recovers the secret at login.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Show slots and whether the login keyring is locked.
.TP
.B list-keys
List keys on connected cards.
.TP
.B enroll
First-time setup.  Asks for the current keyring password (normally the login
password), the card PIN (to prove the card can unwrap the secret) and the login
password for the password slot.
.TP
.B add-piv\fR, \fBadd-fido2
Add another card key or security key, e.g. a backup.
.TP
.B set-password
Re-create the password slot with a card or security key, e.g. after an
administrator reset your password.
.TP
.BI remove " N"
Remove slot N.
.TP
.B unlock
Unlock the running login keyring with a card or security key.
.TP
.B disenroll
Set an ordinary keyring password and delete the wrap file.
.TP
.B zfs-enroll
(root) Change the passphrase of the user's encrypted ZFS home (its own
encryption root, keyformat=passphrase) to the secret, and move the wrap file to
/var/lib/mfa-keyring/\fIuser\fR/ so it is readable before the home is mounted.
Smartcard and FIDO2 logins can then mount the home through pam_zfs_key.
.TP
.B zfs-disenroll
(root) Give the ZFS home an ordinary passphrase again.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-key " ID"
Card key: PKCS#11 id in hex or keyid prefix (8+ hex digits).
.TP
.B \-\-fido2
enroll with a FIDO2 security key.
.TP
.B \-\-uv
FIDO2: also require the security key PIN at every unlock.
.TP
.B \-\-no-password-slot
enroll without a password slot: only the card/key can unlock the keyring.
.TP
.B \-\-force
enroll over an existing wrap file.
.TP
.BI \-\-module " PATH"
PKCS#11 module.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH"
Wrap file.
.TP
.BI \-\-user " USER"
(root) Work on another user's wrap file.  zfs-enroll and zfs-disenroll default
to $SUDO_USER.
.TP
.BI \-\-dataset " NAME"
zfs-enroll: the home dataset (default: the one mounted at the user's home).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pam_mfa_keyring (8)
